'''Tabasco Nahuatl''' or '''Nawat of Tabasco''' is a [[Endangered language|moribund]] [[Nahuan language]] spoken in [[Cupilco]] in the Mexican state of [[Tabasco]].<ref name=e18/>

The language belongs to the eastern branch of the Nahuan language family, and exhibits a number of divergent features.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://nahuatlstudies.blogspot.com/2015/02/tabasco-nawat-not-extinct-nahuan-variety.html |title=Tabasco Nawat: A *not* extinct Nahuatl variety |website=Nawatl Scholar |first=Magnus Pharao |last=Hansen |date=20 February 2015}}</ref>{{Better source needed|date=April 2026}}

