* {{IPAslink|o}} is not common but contasts with {{IPAslink|u}}, e.g., {{lang|nhc|koit}} {{gloss|stick}}, {{lang|nhc|xuit}} {{gloss|year}}. It also appears in loans from [[Ayapa Zoque]], e.g., {{lang|nhc|ooyo}} {{gloss|shrimp}} from {{lang|zoq|óʼyok}} {{gloss|shrimp}}.

Vowel length is contrastive, e.g., {{lang|nhc|istat}} {{gloss|salt}}, {{lang|nhc|istaat}} {{gloss|cotton}}.

